# checks/deps.allow — the reviewed list of everything the product is built from.
#
# The ONLY list checks/no-network.sh compares against (CP-48). One section:
#   cargo:  every name `cargo tree` reports for the workspace, on both Apple-Darwin triples
# The Swift package has no list: it declares no dependency, and checks/no-network.sh fails the run when
# it declares one.
# One name per line, sorted, names only — no versions. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# A change that adds or drops a dependency edits this file in the same commit as the lockfile
# (NFDR QC-26); the comparison fails in both directions, so the list cannot go stale.
#
# What review of THIS file checks, past what the script can (NFDR QC-3, QC-61):
#   - the libgit2 binding (`git2`, `libgit2-sys`) resolves with its HTTPS and SSH features off and
#     libgit2 vendored: `checks/tests/test_no_network.sh` reads both inverse feature trees, and the
#     transport verdict for every name on this list is `checks/deps.review.md`'s (NFDR QC-3);
#   - no crate whose purpose is a TLS or SSH transport (`openssl-sys`, `native-tls`, `rustls`,
#     `libssh2-sys` are examples of that domain, not its membership);
#   - `log` is the one logging facade, with no second facade and no third-party implementation of
#     `log::Log` (`tracing`, `slog`, `log4rs`, `env_logger`, `fern`, `simplelog` likewise examples).

cargo:
aho-corasick
bitflags
cc
equivalent
errno
find-msvc-tools
git2
hashbrown
indexmap
itoa
jobserver
ka-reader-bridge
ka-reader-core
libc
libgit2-sys
libz-sys
log
memchr
pkg-config
proc-macro2
pulldown-cmark
quote
regex
regex-automata
regex-syntax
rustix
serde
serde_core
serde_derive
serde_json
shlex
streaming-iterator
syn
thiserror
thiserror-impl
tree-sitter
tree-sitter-bash
tree-sitter-highlight
tree-sitter-javascript
tree-sitter-json
tree-sitter-language
tree-sitter-python
tree-sitter-toml-ng
tree-sitter-yaml
unicase
unicode-ident
vcpkg
zmij
